<title>CHILE: Chile reports $40.3 mln June trade surplus.</title>
<headline>Chile reports $40.3 mln June trade surplus.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile posted a trade surplus of $40.3 million in June compared with a $5.9 million surplus in the same month 1996, said the Central Bank in its fortnightly report.</p>
<p>Exports rose to $1.4 billion last month from $1.2 billion in June last year.</p>
<p>Imports came to $1.36 billion in June against $1.2 billion in the same month 1996.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
